// A FLEET-MEMBER governed repository, as the parametrized dispatch-path seam
// tests consume it (the adopter-and-member-fixtures bullet of the
// governed-repository integration constraints in `SPECIFICATION/constraints.md`;
// `SPECIFICATION/scenarios.md` Scenario 102).
//
// IT DECLARES NO OPTIONAL INTEGRATION KEY, ON PURPOSE. Every point the schema
// marks optional is left unwritten so the seam tests exercise the FleetDefault
// arm end to end -- which is what "the member fixture passes the same tests on
// fleet defaults" means. The one key written here is `compat.pinned`, which the
// ratified one-resolver clause marks REQUIRED precisely because its only
// substitutable value would be the moving branch tip its own clause forbids: an
// absent pin resolves to `Defective` for a member exactly as it does for an
// adopter, so writing it is what lets the fleet-default arm be the thing under
// test at every other point rather than being masked by a required-field defect.
{
  "livespec-orchestrator-beads-fabro": {
    "compat": {
      "pinned": "v0.109.0"
    }
  }
}
